WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
- All right, before we go,
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.090
I wanna share something super cute

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.470
I found scrolling social media.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.559
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:08.370
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.930
So we talk a lot on this show

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.530
about how we can make kids
more interested in reading.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.440
That's why I love what one
Milwaukee teacher is doing

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.330
to engage his first grade students.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.010
He turns reading and writing

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.200
into catchy, interactive songs

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.508
like his beloved "Punctuation Chant!"

00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:26.341
- Question mark.

00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:28.027
- [Students] Question mark.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.279
- Asks a question.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:30.945
- [Students] Asks a question.

00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:31.778
- How are you?

00:00:31.778 --> 00:00:32.611
- [Students] How are you?

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.493
- Voice lifts up.

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:36.272
- [Students] Voice lifts up.

00:00:36.272 --> 00:00:38.107
- How you doing, friend?

00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:38.940
- [Students] How you doing, friend?

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.520
- Exclamation point!

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.023
- [Students] Exclamation point!

00:00:43.023 --> 00:00:44.410
- Strong and loud.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.776
- [Students] Strong and loud.

00:00:45.776 --> 00:00:46.609
- Hey, you!

00:00:46.609 --> 00:00:47.442
- [Students] Hey, you!

00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:48.275
- Hey, you!

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:49.128
- [Students] Hey, you!

00:00:49.128 --> 00:00:52.430
(audience cheering)
- I love him, adorable.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.540
We have that educator
on the line right now,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.010
watching on TMJ4.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.300
Let's say hi to Jake, y'all.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.557
What's up Jake?
(audience cheering)

00:00:59.557 --> 00:01:01.057
- Hi, how are you?

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.000
- I am so good.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.530
But first and foremost,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.450
thank you so much for being an educator.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.720
We appreciate you so much,
(audience cheering)

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:10.770
value you.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.710
So how did you start with this technique?

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.030
It's very memorable.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:15.863
- Oh my goodness.

00:01:15.863 --> 00:01:16.696
Well, thank you.

00:01:16.696 --> 00:01:20.023
Honestly, so I am a little
bit of an extra person,

00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:21.194
as you can tell,
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:21.194 --> 00:01:22.380
(audience laughing)

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.170
but, honestly, I saw a need for it.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.470
You know, we see some
huge proficiency problems

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.330
in America in reading,

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.100
and the research shows us

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.620
we have to teach the explicit code,

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.450
the sounds and the symbols.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.520
And a lot of people say,
"Well, that's boring,"

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.530
or "That takes the joy away."

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.530
And so I thought, "Well, why
don't we add some motion,

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.470
some songs, and some chants
so that it's not boring."

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.285
And then now here I am.

00:01:48.285 --> 00:01:50.790
(audience laughing)
- I love you so much,

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:51.623
oh my gosh.

00:01:51.623 --> 00:01:54.990
What do the students' parents think?

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:55.890
Do they get involved?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.900
Because if I walked into
my kids' classroom you do,

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.550
I would join, so.
(audience chuckling)

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.670
'Cause I'm also extra, I
don't know if you noticed.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:07.050
- I actually do invite the
parents every month to join in.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.250
So they actually do join
us for phonics every month.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.830
And they get to do the
lesson along with us.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.480
But honestly, Kelly,

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.700
the the sweetest response I've gotten

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.430
is from parents all over the globe.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.850
And it's been like the authenticity piece.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.790
So I don't look like a lot of teachers

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.710
that you would expect in your brain

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.630
when you think of an
elementary teacher, right?

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.850
I act and sound a little different.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.100
And I have so many messages from parents,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.670
like, "Thank you for letting our kids see

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.620
what authenticity is."

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.664
- Oh.
- And so

00:02:41.664 --> 00:02:43.800
it's been like unreal.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.220
I would've never expected
such a outpouring

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.580
of love from parents that have kids

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.920
that maybe feel like they
didn't used to fit in,

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.320
and they can be themselves.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.513
- That is beautiful.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.450
What a beautiful purpose

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.580
other than the major one
you're already doing.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:03.843
Like that's incredible.

00:03:03.843 --> 00:03:06.420
I'm glad that they voiced that as well,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.770
'cause it's very important for everybody

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.140
to feel like, you know, they
fit in somewhere, right,

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.490
And you find your people.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.930
So I'm liking your post

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.640
right now, right?
(bell dings)

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.980
- Yay. Thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.870
- And that's not all, that's not all.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.670
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.880
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.270
want to honor your truly
unstoppable just manner

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.103
and way you teach.

00:03:28.103 --> 00:03:29.160
It's a very beautiful thing.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.000
So what they're gonna do

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.170
is they're just gonna write you a check

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.130
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:32.963
How's that sound?

00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:36.042
(audience cheering)

00:03:38.752 --> 00:03:41.230
- Thank you so much, Jake.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.063
We love you.

00:03:42.063 --> 00:03:44.280
- And thank you to all
our guests this hour,

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.903
Kelsey Grammer, Charles
Melton, M.J. Acosta.

00:03:47.903 --> 00:03:49.075
Y'all have a great day.
(audience cheering)

00:03:49.075 --> 00:03:50.894
If it's not, try and change it.

